{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CevMvsy2QqRRWTPjEDYyk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Conventions this repository already has:**\n- Error handling via `ApiException` subclasses (`ConflictException`, `ResourceNotFoundException`) with enum `ErrorCode`\n- Controllers return `ResponseEntity` with appropriate HTTP status\n- In-memory repositories using `ConcurrentHashMap`\n- Tests use `MockMvc` and verify both status and error envelope structure (the envelope is part of the API contract)\n- Error codes are named after the condition (e.g., `ORDER_NOT_FOUND`, `ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS`)\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `Order.kt` — must add `status` field with enum\n2. `OrderController.kt` — must add cancel endpoint\n3. `ShipmentRepository.kt` — must add method to find shipments by `orderId`\n4. `ShipmentController.kt` — must check if order is cancelled before creating shipment\n5. `ApiError.kt` — must add new error code for cancel conflicts\n6. `OrderControllerTest.kt` — must add tests for cancel behaviour\n7. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — must add test for shipment creation on cancelled order\n\n**Risks:**\n- Order status field is new; existing tests and response structures must adapt\n- All-or-nothing semantics: partial updates on conflict must not happen\n- Idempotency: repeated cancels must not fail\n- Shipment creation must check order status atomically\n\n**Open questions:**\n- What error code should cancellation conflicts use? The ticket names no specific code, only HTTP 409. I'll use a new code `ORDER_CANNOT_CANCEL` to be explicit about the reason.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** — Add `status: OrderStatus` field (enum with `ACTIVE` and `CANCELLED`). New orders default to `ACTIVE`.\n\n2. **OrderStatus.kt** (new file) — Define the `OrderStatus` enum.\n\n3. **ApiError.kt** — Add `ORDER_CANNOT_CANCEL` error code.\n\n4. **ShipmentRepository.kt** — Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` method to query shipments by order.\n\n5. **ShipmentController.kt** — In `create()`, check if the order exists and is not `CANCELLED`. If cancelled, throw `ConflictException` with `ORDER_CANNOT_CANCEL`.\n\n6. **OrderController.kt** — Add `@PostMapping(\"/{orderId}/cancel\")` method that:\n   - Checks if order exists; if not, throw `ResourceNotFoundException`\n   - If order is `CANCELLED`, return it (idempotent)\n   - If order is `ACTIVE`, check all shipments: if any is `CONFIRMED`, throw `ConflictException` (all-or-nothing, no changes)\n   - Otherwise, set order to `CANCELLED`, cancel all `CREATED` shipments, persist, and return the order\n\n7. **OrderControllerTest.kt** — Add tests:\n   - Cancel an `ACTIVE` order → succeeds, order becomes `CANCELLED`, `CREATED` shipments are cancelled\n   - Cancel already-`CANCELLED` order → succeeds, nothing changes\n   - Cancel with `CONFIRMED` shipment → 409, order stays `ACTIVE`, shipments unchanged\n   - Cancel unknown order → 404\n\n8. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add test:\n   - Create shipment for cancelled order → 409\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\n- *In-memory database migration*: Could have initialized all existing orders with `ACTIVE` status on app start, but since repositories are reset in tests via `clear()`, adding the field with a default in the `data class` is simpler and more direct.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Input | Read | Check | Write | Response |\n|------|-------|------|-------|-------|----------|\n| Cancel ACTIVE order | orderId | Order, Shipments by orderId | None with CONFIRMED | Order→CANCELLED, CREATED Shipments→CANCELLED | 200 Order |\n| Cancel CANCELLED order | orderId | Order | — | (nothing) | 200 Order |\n| Cancel with CONFIRMED shipment | orderId | Order, Shipments | ∃ CONFIRMED | (nothing) | 409 ORDER_CANNOT_CANCEL |\n| Unknown order | orderId | — | — | — | 404 ORDER_NOT_FOUND |\n| Create shipment for CANCELLED order | orderId, ... | Order, Shipment | Order.CANCELLED | — | 409 ORDER_CANNOT_CANCEL |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n- `OrderControllerTest.cancel_active_order`: POST cancel on ACTIVE order → 200, status becomes CANCELLED, CREATED shipments cancelled\n- `OrderControllerTest.cancel_already_cancelled`: POST cancel on CANCELLED order → 200, no changes\n- `OrderControllerTest.cancel_with_confirmed_shipment`: POST cancel with CONFIRMED shipment → 409, order stays ACTIVE, shipments unchanged\n- `OrderControllerTest.cancel_unknown_order`: POST cancel on unknown order → 404\n- `ShipmentControllerTest.cannot_create_for_cancelled_order`: POST shipment on CANCELLED order → 409\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes. Let me start by adding the order status enum:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3301,"cache_read_input_tokens":17504,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3301},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7ac732cd-2b93-45a4-b3e4-1dd3366c8a8c","uuid":"951296af-da13-42f8-a3ae-084f64fdcf21","timestamp":"2026-09-10T20:07:17.328Z","request_id":"req_011CevMvsVVjJ7Y6Y92LVZDU"}
